an8.2:2.3 | S: Those venerables reveal what is hidden, clarify what is unclear, and dispel doubt regarding the many doubtful matters. | T: He [the Teacher or the respectable companion in the holy life] reveals what is hidden, makes plain what is obscure, and dispels perplexity in many kinds of perplexing things.
an8.2:2.4 | S: This is the second cause. | T: This is the second cause, the second requisite condition.…
an8.2:3.1 | S: After hearing that teaching they perfect withdrawal of both body and mind. | T: “Having heard the Dhamma, he [the student] achieves a twofold seclusion: seclusion in body & seclusion in mind.
