## an8.40
an8.40:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, the killing of living creatures, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Monks, the taking of life—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:1.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is a short lifespan. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from the taking of life is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to a short life span.
an8.40:2.1 | S: Stealing, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Stealing—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:2.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is loss of wealth. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from stealing is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to the loss of one’s wealth.
an8.40:3.1 | S: Sexual misconduct, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Sexual misconduct—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:3.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is rivalry and enmity. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from sexual misconduct is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to rivalry & revenge.
an8.40:4.1 | S: Lying, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Lying—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:4.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is false accusations. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from lying is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to being falsely accused.
an8.40:5.1 | S: Backbiting, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Divisive speech—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:5.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is being divided against friends. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from divisive speech is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to the breaking of one’s friendships.
an8.40:6.1 | S: Harsh speech, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Harsh speech—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:6.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is hearing disagreeable things. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from harsh speech is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to unappealing sounds.
an8.40:7.1 | S: Talking nonsense, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “Idle chatter—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:7.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is that no one takes what you say seriously. | T: The slightest of all the results coming from idle chatter is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to words that aren’t worth taking to heart.
an8.40:8.1 | S: Drinking beer and wine, when cultivated, developed, and practiced, leads to hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. | T: “The drinking of fermented & distilled liquors—when indulged in, developed, & pursued—is something that leads to hell, leads to rebirth as a common animal, leads to the realm of the hungry ghosts.
an8.40:8.2 | S: The minimum result it leads to for a human being is madness.” | T: The slightest of all the results coming from drinking fermented & distilled liquors is that, when one becomes a human being, it leads to mental derangement.”
an8.40:8.3 | P: Dasamaṁ. | T: (none)
an8.40:8.4 | P: Dānavaggo catuttho. | T: (none)
an8.40:9.0 | P: Tassuddānaṁ | T: (none)
an8.40:9.1 | P: Dve dānāni vatthuñca, | T: (none)
